1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,105
Good evening from the OROS closing desk.

2
00:00:03,105 --> 00:00:09,005
This morning the system named no pick, so tonight there is nothing to grade.

3
00:00:09,005 --> 00:00:13,740
No setup, no trade, no loss — that is the discipline working.

4
00:00:13,740 --> 00:00:18,676
Why we grade in public: a forecast that is never checked is just content.

5
00:00:18,676 --> 00:00:24,085
Every morning call gets an evening verdict, and both go in the permanent record.

6
00:00:24,050 --> 00:00:28,038
On the day, the book is down 907 dollars.

7
00:00:28,038 --> 00:00:35,237
State Street Health Care Select Sector SPDR ETF (XLV) leads, +1.6 percent.

8
00:00:35,237 --> 00:00:40,296
iShares MSCI Emerging Index Fund (EEM) lags at -2.9.

9
00:00:40,296 --> 00:00:45,549
The checklist is clear: nothing requires action today.

10
00:00:45,549 --> 00:00:49,075
On screen, the day's gainers and laggards inside the paper book.

11
00:00:49,031 --> 00:00:56,929
And here is the book itself — the actual holdings, identical to this morning's emailed report.

12
00:00:56,929 --> 00:01:13,313
12 positions, led by State Street SPDR S&P Oil & Gas Exploration & Production ETF, ticker XOP, State Street SPDR S&P Biotech ETF, ticker XBI, Invesco DB Commodity Index Tracking Fund, ticker DBC.

13
00:01:13,313 --> 00:01:24,740
Every line carries its share count, its entry, and its exit — because a position without a defined exit is not a position, it is a hope.

14
00:01:24,697 --> 00:01:29,915
Now the part that makes this system different: the loop.

15
00:01:29,915 --> 00:01:32,523
Every morning OROS proposes.

16
00:01:32,523 --> 00:01:43,983
Every evening it grades its own call, journals the verdict, and adjusts its own risk before it is allowed to propose again.

17
00:01:43,983 --> 00:01:48,269
Inside the book today: 5 positions up, 7 down.

18
00:01:48,269 --> 00:01:50,785
Best, XLE at +1.76 percent.

19
00:01:50,785 --> 00:01:52,742
Worst, ADEA at -5.56.

20
00:01:52,742 --> 00:01:58,145
Both go in the journal — wins and losses get the same ink.

21
00:01:58,145 --> 00:02:05,879
The honest scoreboard reads: expectancy -8.31% per trade over 183 graded positions.

22
00:02:05,879 --> 00:02:13,519
Because that record is soft, the system has throttled itself to 25% position size.

23
00:02:13,519 --> 00:02:19,109
Nobody told it to — full size must be earned back with wins.

24
00:02:19,109 --> 00:02:32,433
What tonight's read hands to tomorrow's open: 34 names close the day in Stage 2; position size stays cut to 25% until the record earns it back.

25
00:02:32,406 --> 00:02:34,578
Over to the sports desk.

26
00:02:34,578 --> 00:02:43,536
Day 32 of the race: three books, the same one hundred thousand simulated dollars, since July sixth.

27
00:02:43,536 --> 00:02:49,599
In first place, the live self-rebuilding book, in blue, at 103,057.

28
00:02:49,599 --> 00:02:54,937
Then the index fund, in gray, 0.9 thousand back at 102,152.

29
00:02:54,937 --> 00:03:01,905
Then the frozen first portfolio, the green line, 3.3 thousand back at 99,762.

30
00:03:01,905 --> 00:03:04,439
The race has no finish line.

31
00:03:04,439 --> 00:03:08,601
Same books, same dollars, back at it tomorrow.

32
00:03:08,601 --> 00:03:13,306
Every line starts the same day with the same dollar.

33
00:03:13,306 --> 00:03:15,116
Nothing is restated.

34
00:03:15,116 --> 00:03:24,024
On screen, three equity lines grown from the same starting dollar: the frozen first book, the live book, and the index fund.

35
00:03:23,986 --> 00:03:31,321
All figures are simulated paper trading, graded and journaled by the OROS agents with no human intervention.

36
00:03:31,321 --> 00:03:33,562
Nothing here is financial advice.

37
00:03:33,562 --> 00:03:36,551
From the closing desk — see you at the open.
